5}{(3-x)}\\cdot \\frac{5}{(3-x)}\\cdot \\frac{5}{(3-x)}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{(\\frac{5}{(3-x)})}^{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{5}{(3-x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-68ccab0f-1b29-5cb7-8904-4a9e96752784"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-68ccab0f-1b29-5cb7-8904-4a9e96752784" :answer-field/id #uuid "68ccab0f-1b29-5cb7-8904-4a9e96752784" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d5d4928e-8cb5-55fe-95ef-93b9144c043b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c9e7c6ec-11ff-55ed-94bd-3c2dc2afe7e8" "answer-7d3024b4-aff7-5c39-87b9-27adafd22f9f" "answer-755dad48-bba6-521d-b6b1-4c1792b0fde6" "answer-4a41c020-4ee4-5481-b86e-95d2d7b1efb3" "answer-d5d4928e-8cb5-55fe-95ef-93b9144c043b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9e7c6ec-11ff-55ed-94bd-3c2dc2afe7e8" :answer/id #uuid "c9e7c6ec-11ff-55ed-94bd-3c2dc2afe7e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10}{(3-x)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d3024b4-aff7-5c39-87b9-27adafd22f9f" :answer/id #uuid "7d3024b4-aff7-5c39-87b9-27adafd22f9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{25}{(3-x)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-755dad48-bba6-521d-b6b1-4c1792b0fde6" :answer/id #uuid "755dad48-bba6-521d-b6b1-4c1792b0fde6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{25}{(3-x)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a41c020-4ee4-5481-b86e-95d2d7b1efb3" :answer/id #uuid "4a41c020-4ee4-5481-b86e-95d2d7b1efb3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{(3-x)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5d4928e-8cb5-55fe-95ef-93b9144c043b" :answer/id #uuid "d5d4928e-8cb5-55fe-95ef-93b9144c043b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{(3-x)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186069942 :tutorial/content "To find the **cube root** of a number $x$, we must ask ourselves, \"what number *cubed* equals $x$?\"\n\nFor example, the cube root of $8$ is $2$ since \n\n$$\n2^3 = 2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2 = 8,\n$$\n\nand the cube root of $-8$ is $-2$ since\n\n$$\n(-2)^3 = (-2) \\cdot (-2) \\cdot (-2) = -8.\n$$\n\nIn general, the cube root of $x^3$ is $x.$\n\nLike the square root, the cube root is signified by a radical symbol, but it also has a little $3$ next to it, i.e., $\\sqrt[3\\!\\phantom{p}]{\\phantom{2}}.$ Using this notation, we can express the above statements mathematically:\n\n- \"The cube root of $8$ is $2$\" can be expressed as $\\sqrt[3]{8}=2.$\n\n- \"The cube root of $-8$ is $-2$\" can be expressed as  $\\sqrt[3]{-8}=-2.$\n\n- \"The cube root of $x^3$ is $x$\" can be expressed as  $\\sqrt[3]{x^3}=x.$\n\n**Note:** For square roots, we have $\\sqrt{x^2} = |x|,$ but for cube roots, we have $\\sqrt[3]{x^3} = x.$ No absolute value is needed for cube roots, because\n\n- the cube root of a positive number is a positive number, and\n\n- the cube root of a negative number is a negative number." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068929 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186197858 :answer-field/choices 17592186197859] [:db/retract 17592186197858 :answer-field/choices 17592186197860] [:db/retract 17592186197858 :answer-field/choices 17592186197861] [:db/retract 17592186197858 :answer-field/choices 17592186197862] [:db/retract 17592186197858 :answer-field/choices 17592186197863] [:db/retract 17592186197834 :answer-field/choices 17592186197835] [:db/retract 17592186197834 :answer-field/choices 17592186197836] [:db/retract 17592186197834 :answer-field/choices 17592186197837] [:db/retract 17592186197834 :answer-field/choices 17592186197838] [:db/retract 17592186197834 :answer-field/choices 17592186197839] {:db/id 17592186198349 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-01982d7c-8631-5513-adcd-2dc3bb87a98b" "question-83fca566-7995-55f0-a5c4-c64563aea218" "question-bf7120f6-4fae-5d19-b842-ba88886669a0" "question-7819f027-d28d-5660-b11c-cd0f95f720fe"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198228 :question/problem "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the ellipsoid $\\dfrac{x^2}{24} + \\dfrac{y^2}{24} +\\dfrac{z^2}{6} = 1$ and the line \n$\\{\\begin{aligned}x=4t \\\\ y=8t, \\\\ z=2t\\end{aligned}$ \nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting the expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ from the parametric equation of the line into the equation of the ellipsoid, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{24}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{24}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{6} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2} & =24 \\\\ (4t)^{2}+(8t)^{2}+4(2t)^{2} & =24 \\\\ 16{t}^{2}+64{t}^{2}+16{t}^{2} & =24 \\\\ 96{t}^{2} & =24 \\\\ {t}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solution $t = \\pm \\dfrac{1}{2}.$ \n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=-\\dfrac 1 2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=4(-\\frac{1}{2})=-2 \\\\ y=8(-\\frac{1}{2})=-4 \\\\ z=2(-\\frac{1}{2})=-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the first point is $\\left(-2,-4,-1\\right).$\n\n- For $t=\\dfrac 1 2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=4(\\frac{1}{2})=2 \\\\ y=8(\\frac{1}{2})=4 \\\\ z=2(\\frac{1}{2})=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the second point is $\\left(2,4,1\\right).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(-2,-4,-1)$ and $(2,4,1).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198433 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-03ac4047-3b67-5e2f-8026-813b5d163c02" "question-04b22284-5add-5373-b896-4f7022795490" "question-925fed75-7149-58ca-b2ab-03e5b43ab0a5" "question-54e46f90-207e-55ef-98ea-cffcdc18e2c7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198075 :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation of our line in the parametric form:\n![](images/b0/b0a31426fa8f1d55dcc4a94fb7b6544cdba753d879a4b95c67b66662ce43a26e.svg)\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\nSubstituting the above expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ (t-1)^{2}+(t+1)^{2} & =(2t)^{2} \\\\ {t}^{2}-2t+1+{t}^{2}+2t+1 & =4{t}^{2} \\\\ 2{t}^{2}+2 & =4{t}^{2} \\\\ 2 & =2{t}^{2} \\\\ {t}^{2} & =1 \\\\ t & =\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=-1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-1-1=-2 \\\\ y=-1+1=0 \\\\ z=2(-1)=-2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the first point is $\\left(-2,0,-2\\right).$\n\n- For $t=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=1-1=0 \\\\ y=1+1=2 \\\\ z=2(1)=2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the second point is $\\left(0,2,2\\right).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(-2,0,-2)$ and $(0,2,2).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198354 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7e565e12-d691-5857-8d63-02efd0af7105" "question-3f2db1db-7bfe-5b3b-ab6d-846d64109b8d" "question-f3934760-11ef-5a3e-86ba-585bb0d00514" "question-58fab8e8-c40a-5f0c-89d7-e35fb797a4f9" "question-75d5fcc2-1404-5925-8c53-e5c58b19a741"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198998 :question/problem "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the ellipsoid $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{6}=1$ and the line \n$\\{\\begin{aligned}x=t \\\\ y=1-t, \\\\ z=t+2\\end{aligned}$ where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting the expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ from the parametric equation of the line into the equation of the ellipsoid, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{6} & =1 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =6 \\\\ 3(t)^{2}+2(1-t)^{2}+(t+2)^{2} & =6 \\\\ 3{t}^{2}+2(1-2t+{t}^{2})+({t}^{2}+4t+4) & =6 \\\\ 6{t}^{2}+6 & =6 \\\\ 6{t}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solution $t=0.$ \n\nNow, we substitute our solution $t=0$ back into the equations of the line.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=0 \\\\ y=1-(0)=1 \\\\ z=(0)+2=2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the point is $(0,1,2).$\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection is $(0,1,2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186197858 :answer-field/correct "answer-e4f6a4fd-f986-5139-9089-efd0086bbe54" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5840fb0f-1558-5ec4-8955-40747a4b4779" "answer-34ef952d-86be-57c3-acf2-24a5e2ed5218" "answer-e4f6a4fd-f986-5139-9089-efd0086bbe54" "answer-7cf06a63-9752-5e5d-8118-e92dea79d7ed" "answer-6e92db24-6441-5216-a2f0-a895392110bf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5840fb0f-1558-5ec4-8955-40747a4b4779" :answer/id #uuid "5840fb0f-1558-5ec4-8955-40747a4b4779" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-1,2,1)$ and $(1,0,3)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-34ef952d-86be-57c3-acf2-24a5e2ed5218" :answer/id #uuid "34ef952d-86be-57c3-acf2-24a5e2ed5218" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,1,2)$ and $(1,0,3)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4f6a4fd-f986-5139-9089-efd0086bbe54" :answer/id #uuid "e4f6a4fd-f986-5139-9089-efd0086bbe54" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,1,2)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7cf06a63-9752-5e5d-8118-e92dea79d7ed" :answer/id #uuid "7cf06a63-9752-5e5d-8118-e92dea79d7ed" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,0,3)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e92db24-6441-5216-a2f0-a895392110bf" :answer/id #uuid "6e92db24-6441-5216-a2f0-a895392110bf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(6,-5,8)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-01982d7c-8631-5513-adcd-2dc3bb87a98b" :question/id #uuid "01982d7c-8631-5513-adcd-2dc3bb87a98b" :question/math-academy-id "q-70494" :question/problem "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=9$ and the line \n$\\{\\begin{aligned}x=t \\\\ y=t-3, \\\\ z=t\\end{aligned}$ where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting the expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ from the parametric equation of the line into the equation of the sphere, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =9 \\\\ (t)^{2}+(t-3)^{2}+(t)^{2} & =9 \\\\ {t}^{2}+({t}^{2}-6t+9)+{t}^{2} & =9 \\\\ 3{t}^{2}-6t+9 & =9 \\\\ 3{t}^{2}-6t & =0 \\\\ t(t-2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $t=0$ and $t=2.$ \n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=0$, we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=(0)=0 \\\\ y=(0)-3=-3 \\\\ z=(0)=0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the first point is $(0,-3,0).$\n\n- For $t=2$, we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=(2)=2 \\\\ y=(2)-3=-1 \\\\ z=(2)=2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the second point is $(2,-1,2).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(0,-3,0)$ and $(2,-1,2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-556152ba-ab4f-5902-a9cf-fccfb5e130ac"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-556152ba-ab4f-5902-a9cf-fccfb5e130ac" :answer-field/id #uuid "556152ba-ab4f-5902-a9cf-fccfb5e130ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bbd52242-1eb0-5bc5-ba5f-f44479a5de55" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bbd52242-1eb0-5bc5-ba5f-f44479a5de55" "answer-88e559ad-8691-5563-bef8-7c758497060e" "answer-4bdbf382-36e1-5d09-9697-08bf328751ea" "answer-f793c3ab-6816-5e62-8e36-6ac1d69a8b67" "answer-2376b38c-9ac7-5ccb-aef2-8febe77582e0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bbd52242-1eb0-5bc5-ba5f-f44479a5de55" :answer/id #uuid "bbd52242-1eb0-5bc5-ba5f-f44479a5de55" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,-3,0)$ and $(2,-1,2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-88e559ad-8691-5563-bef8-7c758497060e" :answer/id #uuid "88e559ad-8691-5563-bef8-7c758497060e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,-1,3)$ and $(-2,1,-2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4bdbf382-36e1-5d09-9697-08bf328751ea" :answer/id #uuid "4bdbf382-36e1-5d09-9697-08bf328751ea" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,-1,3)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f793c3ab-6816-5e62-8e36-6ac1d69a8b67" :answer/id #uuid "f793c3ab-6816-5e62-8e36-6ac1d69a8b67" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,1,3)$ and $(2,1,-2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2376b38c-9ac7-5ccb-aef2-8febe77582e0" :answer/id #uuid "2376b38c-9ac7-5ccb-aef2-8febe77582e0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(2,1,-2)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-83fca566-7995-55f0-a5c4-c64563aea218" :question/id #uuid "83fca566-7995-55f0-a5c4-c64563aea218" :question/math-academy-id "q-73219" :question/problem "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the ellipsoid $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{12}=1$ and the line \n$\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-3t \\\\ y=2t, \\\\ z=-2t\\end{aligned}$ where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting the expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ from the parametric equation of the line into the equation of the ellipsoid, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{12} & =1 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =12 \\\\ 4(-3t)^{2}+2(2t)^{2}+(-2t)^{2} & =12 \\\\ 36{t}^{2}+8{t}^{2}+4{t}^{2} & =12 \\\\ 48{t}^{2} & =12 \\\\ {t}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $t=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $t=\\frac{1}{2}.$ \n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=-\\frac{1}{2}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-3(-\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ y=2(-\\frac{1}{2})=-1 \\\\ z=-2(-\\frac{1}{2})=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the first point is $(\\frac{3}{2},-1,1).$\n\n- For $t=\\frac{1}{2}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-3(\\frac{1}{2})=-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ y=2(\\frac{1}{2})=1 \\\\ z=-2(\\frac{1}{2})=-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the second point is $(-\\frac{3}{2},1,-1).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(\\frac{3}{2},-1,1)$ and $(-\\frac{3}{2},1,-1).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-35c2262e-fd4e-5f1d-8d6d-8e23cdf0a554"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-35c2262e-fd4e-5f1d-8d6d-8e23cdf0a554" :answer-field/id #uuid "35c2262e-fd4e-5f1d-8d6d-8e23cdf0a554" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bd25a088-02c2-5d4e-87e7-de9467e51d93" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fc4a0b05-a807-5c98-96b4-150269a1c9bd" "answer-e75b5a59-d2cd-5446-ad00-5a6bf90899b8" "answer-bd25a088-02c2-5d4e-87e7-de9467e51d93" "answer-912fa47f-946c-5b4e-a27c-271bcf02a4d2" "answer-8caf6956-74b3-5656-bd1b-037cc3f8bd27"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc4a0b05-a807-5c98-96b4-150269a1c9bd" :answer/id #uuid "fc4a0b05-a807-5c98-96b4-150269a1c9bd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(3,-2,2)$ and $(-3,2,-2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e75b5a59-d2cd-5446-ad00-5a6bf90899b8" :answer/id #uuid "e75b5a59-d2cd-5446-ad00-5a6bf90899b8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(3,-2,2)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd25a088-02c2-5d4e-87e7-de9467e51d93" :answer/id #uuid "bd25a088-02c2-5d4e-87e7-de9467e51d93" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(\\frac{3}{2},-1,1)$ and $(-\\frac{3}{2},1,-1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-912fa47f-946c-5b4e-a27c-271bcf02a4d2" :answer/id #uuid "912fa47f-946c-5b4e-a27c-271bcf02a4d2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(\\frac{3}{2},-1,1)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8caf6956-74b3-5656-bd1b-037cc3f8bd27" :answer/id #uuid "8caf6956-74b3-5656-bd1b-037cc3f8bd27" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(\\frac{3}{2},1,1)$ and $(-\\frac{3}{2},-1,-1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bf7120f6-4fae-5d19-b842-ba88886669a0" :question/id #uuid "bf7120f6-4fae-5d19-b842-ba88886669a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-71129" :question/problem "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the ellipsoid $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}=1$ and the line \n$\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2t \\\\ y=2-t, \\\\ z=t-1\\end{aligned}$ where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting the expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ from the parametric equation of the line into the equation of the ellipsoid, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2} & =8 \\\\ (2t)^{2}+4(2-t)^{2}+2(t-1)^{2} & =8 \\\\ 4{t}^{2}+4(4-4t+{t}^{2})+2({t}^{2}-2t+1) & =8 \\\\ 4{t}^{2}+16-16t+4{t}^{2}+2{t}^{2}-4t+2 & =8 \\\\ 10{t}^{2}-20t+18 & =8 \\\\ 10{t}^{2}-20t+10 & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2}-2t+1 & =0 \\\\ (t-1)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solution $t=1.$\n\nNow, we substitute our solution back into the equations of the line.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2(1)=2 \\\\ y=2-1=1 \\\\ z=1-1=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection is $(2,1,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2f0fad20-662a-5ac9-aa37-fdaf4bd1c44b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2f0fad20-662a-5ac9-aa37-fdaf4bd1c44b" :answer-field/id #uuid "2f0fad20-662a-5ac9-aa37-fdaf4bd1c44b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-19504466-0a10-574f-bb8c-3c8ded8f176c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-85fe0a6f-92b1-5ed1-85c4-d3ebde706c06" "answer-476cbccb-7f02-581b-b415-12ad49fd0514" "answer-85f544ac-b2af-53d2-9846-ab93a0ca63da" "answer-3402b0ae-2770-548b-bd7e-08caf8efcf00" "answer-19504466-0a10-574f-bb8c-3c8ded8f176c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-85fe0a6f-92b1-5ed1-85c4-d3ebde706c06" :answer/id #uuid "85fe0a6f-92b1-5ed1-85c4-d3ebde706c06" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-2,3,-2)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-476cbccb-7f02-581b-b415-12ad49fd0514" :answer/id #uuid "476cbccb-7f02-581b-b415-12ad49fd0514" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,2,-1)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-85f544ac-b2af-53d2-9846-ab93a0ca63da" :answer/id #uuid "85f544ac-b2af-53d2-9846-ab93a0ca63da" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(2,-1,1)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3402b0ae-2770-548b-bd7e-08caf8efcf00" :answer/id #uuid "3402b0ae-2770-548b-bd7e-08caf8efcf00" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(2,1,0)$ and $(-2,3,-2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19504466-0a10-574f-bb8c-3c8ded8f176c" :answer/id #uuid "19504466-0a10-574f-bb8c-3c8ded8f176c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(2,1,0)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7819f027-d28d-5660-b11c-cd0f95f720fe" :question/id #uuid "7819f027-d28d-5660-b11c-cd0f95f720fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-70957" :question/problem "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the sphere $(x-1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}+{z}^{2}=36$ and the line \n$\\{\\begin{aligned}x=t+1 \\\\ y=2t+2, \\\\ z=t+6\\end{aligned}$ where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting the expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ from the parametric equation of the line into the equation of the sphere, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =36 \\\\ {((t+1)-1)}^{2}+{((2t+2)-2)}^{2}+{(t+6)}^{2} & =36 \\\\ {t}^{2}+4{t}^{2}+({t}^{2}+12t+36) & =36 \\\\ 6{t}^{2}+12t+36 & =36 \\\\ 6{t}^{2}+12t & =0 \\\\ t(t+2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $t=0$ and $t=-2.$ \n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=0$, we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=(0)+1=1 \\\\ y=2(0)+2=2 \\\\ z=(0)+6=6,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the first point is $(1,2,6).$\n\n- For $t=-2$, we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=(-2)+1=-1 \\\\ y=2(-2)+2=-2 \\\\ z=(-2)+6=4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the second point is $(-1,-2,4).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(1,2,6)$ and $(-1,-2,4).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-88c428fa-eb9a-5abc-94ad-cb031dd35e32"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-88c428fa-eb9a-5abc-94ad-cb031dd35e32" :answer-field/id #uuid "88c428fa-eb9a-5abc-94ad-cb031dd35e32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9738f5d5-30f2-54f5-b519-04f2dece2bdb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-822195d9-b4ca-5da4-a47f-e77424f2c224" "answer-d1da9504-c5b6-53eb-a566-9e371e654451" "answer-68903205-36b5-5e27-95f6-4876748a4c2e" "answer-9738f5d5-30f2-54f5-b519-04f2dece2bdb" "answer-20daa437-703f-5c1f-bfef-06c613eae5d1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-822195d9-b4ca-5da4-a47f-e77424f2c224" :answer/id #uuid "822195d9-b4ca-5da4-a47f-e77424f2c224" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-1,2,2)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d1da9504-c5b6-53eb-a566-9e371e654451" :answer/id #uuid "d1da9504-c5b6-53eb-a566-9e371e654451" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,-2,-4)$ and $(1,0,4)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-68903205-36b5-5e27-95f6-4876748a4c2e" :answer/id #uuid "68903205-36b5-5e27-95f6-4876748a4c2e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,-2,-4)$ and $(1,2,-6)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9738f5d5-30f2-54f5-b519-04f2dece2bdb" :answer/id #uuid "9738f5d5-30f2-54f5-b519-04f2dece2bdb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,2,6)$ and $(-1,-2,4)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20daa437-703f-5c1f-bfef-06c613eae5d1" :answer/id #uuid "20daa437-703f-5c1f-bfef-06c613eae5d1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(3,6,-4)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-03ac4047-3b67-5e2f-8026-813b5d163c02" :question/id #uuid "03ac4047-3b67-5e2f-8026-813b5d163c02" :question/math-academy-id "q-94783" :question/problem "Find the points of the intersection of the elliptic cone $2{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}={z}^{2}$ and the line $x-2=y+1=\\frac{z}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation of our line in the parametric form:\n\n$$\nx-2=y+1=\\frac{z}{3}=t\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}x=t+2 \\\\ y=t-1 \\\\ z=3t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSubstituting the above expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ 2(t+2)^{2}+4(t-1)^{2} & =(3t)^{2} \\\\ 2({t}^{2}+4t+4)+4({t}^{2}-2t+1) & =9{t}^{2} \\\\ 2{t}^{2}+8t+8+4{t}^{2}-8t+4 & =9{t}^{2} \\\\ 3{t}^{2}-12 & =0 \\\\ 3({t}^{2}-4) & =0 \\\\ 3(t+2)(t-2) & =0 \\\\ t & =\\pm 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=-2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-2+2=0 \\\\ y=-2-1=-3 \\\\ z=3(-2)=-6,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the first point is $(0,-3,-6).$\n\n- For $t=2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2+2=4 \\\\ y=2-1=1 \\\\ z=3(2)=6,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the second point is $(4,1,6).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(0,-3,-6)$ and $(4,1,6).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-101a7658-6522-5e95-9874-dab42cc55c4a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-101a7658-6522-5e95-9874-dab42cc55c4a" :answer-field/id #uuid "101a7658-6522-5e95-9874-dab42cc55c4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f7c4ccfd-f5ea-5cea-a5ac-62d7e712889c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f7c4ccfd-f5ea-5cea-a5ac-62d7e712889c" "answer-b1ce6c4c-4c00-5d76-8918-0c25150319f1" "answer-158e4055-a575-5687-b6c0-7b18540160c9" "answer-9d644e50-890f-5bbd-af2c-3c7931490a82" "answer-c8e98c45-0e9a-57dc-a49d-771e71132536"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7c4ccfd-f5ea-5cea-a5ac-62d7e712889c" :answer/id #uuid "f7c4ccfd-f5ea-5cea-a5ac-62d7e712889c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,-3,-6)$ and $(4,1,6)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1ce6c4c-4c00-5d76-8918-0c25150319f1" :answer/id #uuid "b1ce6c4c-4c00-5d76-8918-0c25150319f1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,-3,-6)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-158e4055-a575-5687-b6c0-7b18540160c9" :answer/id #uuid "158e4055-a575-5687-b6c0-7b18540160c9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(2,-1,0)$ and $(3,0,3)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d644e50-890f-5bbd-af2c-3c7931490a82" :answer/id #uuid "9d644e50-890f-5bbd-af2c-3c7931490a82" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(2,-1,0)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c8e98c45-0e9a-57dc-a49d-771e71132536" :answer/id #uuid "c8e98c45-0e9a-57dc-a49d-771e71132536" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(4,1,6)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-04b22284-5add-5373-b896-4f7022795490" :question/id #uuid "04b22284-5add-5373-b896-4f7022795490" :question/math-academy-id "q-94775" :question/problem "Find the points of the intersection of the elliptic cone $2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={z}^{2}$ and the line $x+1=y-1=\\frac{z}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation of our line in the parametric form:\n\n$$\nx+1=y-1=\\frac{z}{2}=t\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}x=t-1 \\\\ y=t+1 \\\\ z=2t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSubstituting the above expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ 2(t-1)^{2}+(t+1)^{2} & =(2t)^{2} \\\\ 2({t}^{2}-2t+1)+({t}^{2}+2t+1) & =4{t}^{2} \\\\ 2{t}^{2}-4t+2+{t}^{2}+2t+1 & =4{t}^{2} \\\\ {t}^{2}+2t-3 & =0 \\\\ (t+3)(t-1) & =0 \\\\ t & =-3,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=-3,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-3-1=-4 \\\\ y=-3+1=-2 \\\\ z=2(-3)=-6,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the first point is $(-4,-2,-6).$\n\n- For $t=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=1-1=0 \\\\ y=1+1=2 \\\\ z=2(1)=2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the second point is $(0,2,2).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(-4,-2,-6)$ and $(0,2,2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-89359ee7-4c2c-57c0-acaa-381ae6084719"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-89359ee7-4c2c-57c0-acaa-381ae6084719" :answer-field/id #uuid "89359ee7-4c2c-57c0-acaa-381ae6084719" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a40e8f00-f264-53cd-9903-d88fc84da7bd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-56d19d92-5983-5fc3-a97b-e1328867bdf8" "answer-a40e8f00-f264-53cd-9903-d88fc84da7bd" "answer-381612bb-bf1f-5b5d-9e4f-e8deacf09159" "answer-1937aa4c-02a1-520f-b072-f81c55825fc1" "answer-74bc61bc-347a-5065-bb28-0f6dc479bcdf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56d19d92-5983-5fc3-a97b-e1328867bdf8" :answer/id #uuid "56d19d92-5983-5fc3-a97b-e1328867bdf8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-2,0,-2)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a40e8f00-f264-53cd-9903-d88fc84da7bd" :answer/id #uuid "a40e8f00-f264-53cd-9903-d88fc84da7bd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-4,-2,-6)$ and $(0,2,2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-381612bb-bf1f-5b5d-9e4f-e8deacf09159" :answer/id #uuid "381612bb-bf1f-5b5d-9e4f-e8deacf09159" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-4,-2,-6)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1937aa4c-02a1-520f-b072-f81c55825fc1" :answer/id #uuid "1937aa4c-02a1-520f-b072-f81c55825fc1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,2,2)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74bc61bc-347a-5065-bb28-0f6dc479bcdf" :answer/id #uuid "74bc61bc-347a-5065-bb28-0f6dc479bcdf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(2,4,6)$ and $(-2,0,-2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198994 :question/problem "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the ellipsoid $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{27}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3}=1$ and the line $\\frac{x-3}{3}=y-1=z-1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation of our line in parametric form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{3}=y-1=z-1=t\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}x=3t+3 \\\\ y=t+1 \\\\ z=t+1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSubstituting the above expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ into the equation of the ellipsoid, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{27}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}+9{z}^{2} & =27 \\\\ (3t+3)^{2}+9(t+1)^{2}+9(t+1)^{2} & =27 \\\\ (9{t}^{2}+18t+9)+9({t}^{2}+2t+1)+9({t}^{2}+2t+1) & =27 \\\\ 27{t}^{2}+54t+27 & =27 \\\\ 27{t}^{2}+54t & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2}+2t & =0 \\\\ t(t+2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $t=0$ and $t=-2.$ \n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=0$, we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=3(0)+3=3 \\\\ y=(0)+1=1 \\\\ z=(0)+1=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the first point is $(3,1,1).$\n\n- For $t=-2$, we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=3(-2)+3=-3 \\\\ y=(-2)+1=-1 \\\\ z=(-2)+1=-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the second point is $(-3,-1,-1).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(3,1,1)$ and $(-3,-1,-1).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186197834 :answer-field/correct "answer-3e2c38b2-bd40-5fb8-9dcb-029898ecb5a6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3418e24d-c46a-5074-853c-a90a5378e76c" "answer-096c9c95-3d61-58ff-a3ab-a51f804213af" "answer-df58b652-b996-5398-9e5e-cd540b98ba8d" "answer-3e2c38b2-bd40-5fb8-9dcb-029898ecb5a6" "answer-7310d89c-868c-5739-8a05-2f80cc315acd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3418e24d-c46a-5074-853c-a90a5378e76c" :answer/id #uuid "3418e24d-c46a-5074-853c-a90a5378e76c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-3,1,-1)$ and $(3,-1,1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-096c9c95-3d61-58ff-a3ab-a51f804213af" :answer/id #uuid "096c9c95-3d61-58ff-a3ab-a51f804213af" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-3,1,1)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df58b652-b996-5398-9e5e-cd540b98ba8d" :answer/id #uuid "df58b652-b996-5398-9e5e-cd540b98ba8d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(3,-1,-1)$ and $(-3,1,1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e2c38b2-bd40-5fb8-9dcb-029898ecb5a6" :answer/id #uuid "3e2c38b2-bd40-5fb8-9dcb-029898ecb5a6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(3,1,1)$ and $(-3,-1,-1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7310d89c-868c-5739-8a05-2f80cc315acd" :answer/id #uuid "7310d89c-868c-5739-8a05-2f80cc315acd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(3,1,1)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-925fed75-7149-58ca-b2ab-03e5b43ab0a5" :question/id #uuid "925fed75-7149-58ca-b2ab-03e5b43ab0a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-70960" :question/problem "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the sphere ${x}^{2}+(y+7)^{2}+(z+1)^{2}=81$ and the line $-\\frac{x}{2}=2-y=\\frac{z+1}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation of our line in parametric form:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{x}{2}=\\frac{2-y}{1}=\\frac{z+1}{2}=t\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-2t \\\\ y=2-t \\\\ z=2t-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSubstituting the above expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ into the equation of the sphere, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+(y-1)^{2}+(z+1)^{2} & =81 \\\\ (-2t)^{2}+((2-t)+7)^{2}+((2t-1)+1)^{2} & =81 \\\\ (-2t)^{2}+(9-t)^{2}+(2t)^{2} & =81 \\\\ 4{t}^{2}+(81-18t+{t}^{2})+4{t}^{2} & =81 \\\\ 9{t}^{2}-18t+81 & =81 \\\\ 9{t}^{2}-18t & =0 \\\\ t(t-2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $t=0$ and $t=2.$ \n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=0$, we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-2(0)=0 \\\\ y=2-(0)=2 \\\\ z=2(0)-1=-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the first point is $(0,2,-1).$\n\n- For $t=2$, we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-2(2)=-4 \\\\ y=2-(2)=0 \\\\ z=2(2)-1=3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the second point is $(-4,0,3).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(0,2,-1)$ and $(-4,0,3).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-54918cdd-65dd-5ee0-a8b6-130e964c1af0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-54918cdd-65dd-5ee0-a8b6-130e964c1af0" :answer-field/id #uuid "54918cdd-65dd-5ee0-a8b6-130e964c1af0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9e5dd78a-f677-56eb-95e4-42454a1b37a8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-86bb3f55-b716-5227-b073-df61629436e9" "answer-9e5dd78a-f677-56eb-95e4-42454a1b37a8" "answer-720db885-be87-54a4-99e5-45e7d112bf6c" "answer-874b5494-11c0-50b9-8a3b-77cc02ec2985" "answer-338b118d-9bea-5bd0-994b-399c71333888"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-86bb3f55-b716-5227-b073-df61629436e9" :answer/id #uuid "86bb3f55-b716-5227-b073-df61629436e9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-4,2,-1)$ and $(0,0,3)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9e5dd78a-f677-56eb-95e4-42454a1b37a8" :answer/id #uuid "9e5dd78a-f677-56eb-95e4-42454a1b37a8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,2,-1)$ and $(-4,0,3)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-720db885-be87-54a4-99e5-45e7d112bf6c" :answer/id #uuid "720db885-be87-54a4-99e5-45e7d112bf6c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,2,-4)$ and $(-1,0,3)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-874b5494-11c0-50b9-8a3b-77cc02ec2985" :answer/id #uuid "874b5494-11c0-50b9-8a3b-77cc02ec2985" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,2,0)$ and $(-4,-1,3)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-338b118d-9bea-5bd0-994b-399c71333888" :answer/id #uuid "338b118d-9bea-5bd0-994b-399c71333888" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,3,-1)$ and $(-4,0,2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-54e46f90-207e-55ef-98ea-cffcdc18e2c7" :question/id #uuid "54e46f90-207e-55ef-98ea-cffcdc18e2c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-71960" :question/problem "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the sphere $(x+1)^{2}+{y}^{2}+(z-2)^{2}=100$ and the line $\\frac{x-5}{2}=-y=z+6.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation of our line in parametric form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-5}{2}=\\frac{y}{-1}=\\frac{z+6}{1}=t\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2t+5 \\\\ y=-t \\\\ z=t-6,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSubstituting the above expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ into the equation of the sphere, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2}+{y}^{2}+(z-2)^{2} & =100 \\\\ ((2t+5)+1)^{2}+(-t)^{2}+((t-6)-2)^{2} & =100 \\\\ (2t+6)^{2}+(-t)^{2}+(t-8)^{2} & =100 \\\\ (4{t}^{2}+24t+36)+{t}^{2}+({t}^{2}-16t+64) & =100 \\\\ 6{t}^{2}+8t+100 & =100 \\\\ 6{t}^{2}+8t & =0 \\\\ 2t(3t+4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $t=0$ and $t=-\\frac{4}{3}.$ \n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=0$, we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2(0)+5=5 \\\\ y=-(0)=0 \\\\ z=(0)-6=-6,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the first point is $(5,0,-6).$\n\n- For $t=-\\frac{4}{3}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2(-\\frac{4}{3})+5=\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ y=-(-\\frac{4}{3})=\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ z=(-\\frac{4}{3})-6=-\\frac{22}{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the second point is $(\\frac{7}{3},\\frac{4}{3},-\\frac{22}{3}).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(5,0,-6)$ and $(\\frac{7}{3},\\frac{4}{3},-\\frac{22}{3}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8159c22d-ec7f-5de6-bf20-9a2452034f66"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8159c22d-ec7f-5de6-bf20-9a2452034f66" :answer-field/id #uuid "8159c22d-ec7f-5de6-bf20-9a2452034f66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-abc3bbc9-dc43-572e-9953-c02ca742e1c9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-19af1e47-b0c8-5aa5-8bb9-46eef20e668a" "answer-84798499-fed0-5ab8-b453-9364e7bc3bc9" "answer-89e0e314-6093-5699-85bc-bf6985a0acec" "answer-f1340dfa-8a97-5e37-b745-f69f2cf865bc" "answer-abc3bbc9-dc43-572e-9953-c02ca742e1c9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19af1e47-b0c8-5aa5-8bb9-46eef20e668a" :answer/id #uuid "19af1e47-b0c8-5aa5-8bb9-46eef20e668a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(5,0,-6)$ and $(-1,-3,-9)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84798499-fed0-5ab8-b453-9364e7bc3bc9" :answer/id #uuid "84798499-fed0-5ab8-b453-9364e7bc3bc9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(5,0,-6)$ and $(-3,-4,-10)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-89e0e314-6093-5699-85bc-bf6985a0acec" :answer/id #uuid "89e0e314-6093-5699-85bc-bf6985a0acec" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(5,0,-6)$ and $(\\frac{23}{3},-\\frac{4}{3},-\\frac{14}{3})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1340dfa-8a97-5e37-b745-f69f2cf865bc" :answer/id #uuid "f1340dfa-8a97-5e37-b745-f69f2cf865bc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(5,0,-6)$ and $(\\frac{7}{3},\\frac{4}{3},-\\frac{14}{3})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-abc3bbc9-dc43-572e-9953-c02ca742e1c9" :answer/id #uuid "abc3bbc9-dc43-572e-9953-c02ca742e1c9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(5,0,-6)$ and $(\\frac{7}{3},\\frac{4}{3},-\\frac{22}{3})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7e565e12-d691-5857-8d63-02efd0af7105" :question/id #uuid "7e565e12-d691-5857-8d63-02efd0af7105" :question/math-academy-id "q-72337" :question/problem "Find the projection of the intersection between the elliptic paraboloid $z-4=(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}$ and the plane $x+y=-4$ onto $yz$-plane." :question/worked-solution "Since we want to find the projection onto the $yz$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $x.$ First, we solve for $x$ in the equation of the plane, as follows:\n\n$$\nx+y=-4\\,⟹\\,x=-4-y\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $x$ into the equation of the paraboloid, we obtain: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-4 & =((-4-y)-2)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} \\\\ z-4 & =(-y-6)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} \\\\ z-4 & ={y}^{2}+12y+36+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} \\\\ z-4 & =\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2}+12x+36 \\\\ z-4 & =\\frac{3}{2}({y}^{2}+8y+24) \\\\ z-4 & =\\frac{3}{2}(({y}^{2}+8y+16)+8) \\\\ z-4 & =\\frac{3}{2}(y+4)^{2}+12 \\\\ z & =\\frac{3}{2}(y+4)^{2}+16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the projection of the intersection is the parabola $z=\\frac{3}{2}(y+4)^{2}+16.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-44cb9f95-73e3-524a-827d-1a98148e129a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-44cb9f95-73e3-524a-827d-1a98148e129a" :answer-field/id #uuid "44cb9f95-73e3-524a-827d-1a98148e129a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8db83346-df15-571a-88b3-9ec53b42513e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5f664acd-0f58-51a7-829f-fb2b4bf1c158" "answer-8db83346-df15-571a-88b3-9ec53b42513e" "answer-16bd4c4d-53a0-526b-814f-cc329822f5c2" "answer-f2a7669c-5d9a-56be-933a-d77f93c3f227" "answer-210e1ce3-5722-50b6-b4c8-4929dd75f7d3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f664acd-0f58-51a7-829f-fb2b4bf1c158" :answer/id #uuid "5f664acd-0f58-51a7-829f-fb2b4bf1c158" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\frac{3}{2}(y+4)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8db83346-df15-571a-88b3-9ec53b42513e" :answer/id #uuid "8db83346-df15-571a-88b3-9ec53b42513e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\frac{3}{2}(y+4)^{2}+16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16bd4c4d-53a0-526b-814f-cc329822f5c2" :answer/id #uuid "16bd4c4d-53a0-526b-814f-cc329822f5c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\frac{3}{2}(y-4)^{2}+12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2a7669c-5d9a-56be-933a-d77f93c3f227" :answer/id #uuid "f2a7669c-5d9a-56be-933a-d77f93c3f227" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\frac{3}{2}(y-4)^{2}+16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-210e1ce3-5722-50b6-b4c8-4929dd75f7d3" :answer/id #uuid "210e1ce3-5722-50b6-b4c8-4929dd75f7d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3f2db1db-7bfe-5b3b-ab6d-846d64109b8d" :question/id #uuid "3f2db1db-7bfe-5b3b-ab6d-846d64109b8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-72342" :question/problem "For the elliptic paraboloid $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{5}=z+4$, the section in the plane $\\sqrt{5}x+4y=4$ is a parabola. \nFind the vertex of the projection of this parabola onto $yz$-plane." :question/worked-solution "Since we want to find the projection onto the $yz$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $x.$ First, we solve for $x$ in the equation of the plane, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{5}x+4y=4\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{4-4y}{\\sqrt{5}}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $x$ into the equation of the paraboloid, we obtain: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{(\\frac{4-4y}{\\sqrt{5}})}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{5} & =z+4 \\\\ \\frac{4(1-y)^{2}}{5}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{5} & =z+4 \\\\ (y-1)^{2} & =z+4 \\\\ z & =(y-1)^{2}-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the vertex of the projection onto $yz$-plane is $(1,-4).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bf6552b0-6071-5cb6-8a4f-6d1b9d70cb89"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bf6552b0-6071-5cb6-8a4f-6d1b9d70cb89" :answer-field/id #uuid "bf6552b0-6071-5cb6-8a4f-6d1b9d70cb89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8eb0748f-88f4-5a20-a136-b18b07e72b94" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5a3c9888-3e12-5f64-b8ce-fec1d37e0fa4" "answer-3a93ae61-117e-52eb-a561-05bda1830dfe" "answer-a1b4f9f0-5d69-54f2-a20f-cb95071368a0" "answer-8eb0748f-88f4-5a20-a136-b18b07e72b94" "answer-3fa19c57-773f-538a-8210-ed0794e91c6d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a3c9888-3e12-5f64-b8ce-fec1d37e0fa4" :answer/id #uuid "5a3c9888-3e12-5f64-b8ce-fec1d37e0fa4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-1,-4)$ in the $yz$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3a93ae61-117e-52eb-a561-05bda1830dfe" :answer/id #uuid "3a93ae61-117e-52eb-a561-05bda1830dfe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-1,4)$ in the $yz$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1b4f9f0-5d69-54f2-a20f-cb95071368a0" :answer/id #uuid "a1b4f9f0-5d69-54f2-a20f-cb95071368a0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-4,1)$ in the $yz$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8eb0748f-88f4-5a20-a136-b18b07e72b94" :answer/id #uuid "8eb0748f-88f4-5a20-a136-b18b07e72b94" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,-4)$ in the $yz$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3fa19c57-773f-538a-8210-ed0794e91c6d" :answer/id #uuid "3fa19c57-773f-538a-8210-ed0794e91c6d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,4)$ in the $yz$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f3934760-11ef-5a3e-86ba-585bb0d00514" :question/id #uuid "f3934760-11ef-5a3e-86ba-585bb0d00514" :question/math-academy-id "q-70555" :question/problem "Find the projection of the intersection between the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=10$ and the plane $z-y=2$ onto the $xy$-plane." :question/worked-solution "Since we want to find the projection onto the $xy$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $z.$ First, we solve for $z$ in the equation of the plane, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-y & =2\\,⟹\\,z=2+y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $z$ into the equation of the sphere, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =10 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+(2+y)^{2} & =10 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+(4+4y+{y}^{2}) & =10 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+4y+4 & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by completing the square for the variable $y$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+4y+4 & =10 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+2 & =8 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2({y}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+1) & =8 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2(y+1)^{2} & =8 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{4} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the projection of the intersection is the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{4}=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e38aa8a0-730c-5f61-9672-fbfd36ec5e9b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e38aa8a0-730c-5f61-9672-fbfd36ec5e9b" :answer-field/id #uuid "e38aa8a0-730c-5f61-9672-fbfd36ec5e9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5f8af2ed-6ade-5c05-8444-37e9f2e4600a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-84d0a98a-843f-5cff-ab9b-d8f9b4d153b5" "answer-f2c21e1a-675b-58de-a749-fcf9249347a1" "answer-ff15e463-523f-56d5-be3c-4a291647e90e" "answer-0ec7c4e7-0717-579f-af46-0ad1c775388d" "answer-5f8af2ed-6ade-5c05-8444-37e9f2e4600a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84d0a98a-843f-5cff-ab9b-d8f9b4d153b5" :answer/id #uuid "84d0a98a-843f-5cff-ab9b-d8f9b4d153b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2c21e1a-675b-58de-a749-fcf9249347a1" :answer/id #uuid "f2c21e1a-675b-58de-a749-fcf9249347a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff15e463-523f-56d5-be3c-4a291647e90e" :answer/id #uuid "ff15e463-523f-56d5-be3c-4a291647e90e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{4}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ec7c4e7-0717-579f-af46-0ad1c775388d" :answer/id #uuid "0ec7c4e7-0717-579f-af46-0ad1c775388d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{4}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f8af2ed-6ade-5c05-8444-37e9f2e4600a" :answer/id #uuid "5f8af2ed-6ade-5c05-8444-37e9f2e4600a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{4}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-58fab8e8-c40a-5f0c-89d7-e35fb797a4f9" :question/id #uuid "58fab8e8-c40a-5f0c-89d7-e35fb797a4f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-94954" :question/problem "Which of the following best describes the projection of the intersection between the elliptic cone $2{x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=2(z-2)^{2}$ and the plane $2z-x-10=0$ onto the $xy$-plane?" :question/worked-solution "Since we want to find the projection onto the $xy$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $z.$ First, we solve the equation of the plane for $z,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n2z-x-10=0\\,⟹\\,z=\\frac{x}{2}+5\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $z$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =2{(\\frac{x}{2}+5-2)}^{2} \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =2{(\\frac{x}{2}+3)}^{2} \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =2(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+3x+9) \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+6x+18 \\\\ \\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}-6x+(y+3)^{2} & =18 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}({x}^{2}-4x+4)-6+(y+3)^{2} & =18 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}{(x-2)}^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =24 \\\\ \\frac{{(x-2)}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{24} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of an ellipse centered at $(2,-3)$ in the $xy$-plane." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7d014e84-90ae-55bd-8e44-eb912baf0075"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7d014e84-90ae-55bd-8e44-eb912baf0075" :answer-field/id #uuid "7d014e84-90ae-55bd-8e44-eb912baf0075" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fa27f81e-26da-55b9-b7c4-542c280c96da" :answer-field/choices ["answer-628b083b-64e7-5523-9a16-b836f553e8fe" "answer-70cc3d86-a276-51ae-b8d9-d32a97d5be00" "answer-f7d182d3-ab5c-58a8-aa85-15afb61de658" "answer-fbe86de5-9b39-5b64-9487-3456434b86bb" "answer-fa27f81e-26da-55b9-b7c4-542c280c96da"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-628b083b-64e7-5523-9a16-b836f553e8fe" :answer/id #uuid "628b083b-64e7-5523-9a16-b836f553e8fe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A hyperbola centered at $(2,-3)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70cc3d86-a276-51ae-b8d9-d32a97d5be00" :answer/id #uuid "70cc3d86-a276-51ae-b8d9-d32a97d5be00" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A hyperbola centered at $(3,-2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7d182d3-ab5c-58a8-aa85-15afb61de658" :answer/id #uuid "f7d182d3-ab5c-58a8-aa85-15afb61de658" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A parabola centered at $(-3,-2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fbe86de5-9b39-5b64-9487-3456434b86bb" :answer/id #uuid "fbe86de5-9b39-5b64-9487-3456434b86bb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An ellipse centered at $(0,3)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa27f81e-26da-55b9-b7c4-542c280c96da" :answer/id #uuid "fa27f81e-26da-55b9-b7c4-542c280c96da" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An ellipse centered at $(2,-3)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-75d5fcc2-1404-5925-8c53-e5c58b19a741" :question/id #uuid "75d5fcc2-1404-5925-8c53-e5c58b19a741" :question/math-academy-id "q-35928" :question/problem "Find the projection of the intersection between the elliptic paraboloid $6z-6={x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}$ and the plane $x+y=2$ onto $yz$-plane." :question/worked-solution "Since we want to find the projection onto the $yz$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $x.$ First, we solve for $x$ in the equation of the plane, as follows:\n\n$$\nx+y=2\\,⟹\\,x=2-y\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $x$ into the equation of the paraboloid, we obtain: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2-y)^{2}+3{y}^{2} & =6z-6 \\\\ {y}^{2}-4y+4+3{y}^{2} & =6z-6 \\\\ 6z-6 & =4{y}^{2}-4y+4 \\\\ 6z-6 & =4({y}^{2}-y+1) \\\\ 6z-6 & =4{(y-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+3 \\\\ 6z & =4{(y-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+9 \\\\ z & =\\frac{2}{3}{(y-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the projection of the intersection is the parabola $z=\\frac{2}{3}{(y-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{3}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-13a502e6-ea44-5bb6-a268-5801b7bef457"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-13a502e6-ea44-5bb6-a268-5801b7bef457" :answer-field/id #uuid "13a502e6-ea44-5bb6-a268-5801b7bef457" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-781c4a5e-6128-5f7c-8d4d-bc8159e4a2de" :answer-field/choices ["answer-71de7fc3-0756-5137-bb21-59702b351d65" "answer-06b975fd-e446-5a55-b271-ff62ed2f207d" "answer-563e7933-88b2-5d09-a466-e815264e47b5" "answer-781c4a5e-6128-5f7c-8d4d-bc8159e4a2de" "answer-e5de6f57-ca27-538b-8d1c-dacfab40980e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-71de7fc3-0756-5137-bb21-59702b351d65" :answer/id #uuid "71de7fc3-0756-5137-bb21-59702b351d65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=4{(y-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06b975fd-e446-5a55-b271-ff62ed2f207d" :answer/id #uuid "06b975fd-e446-5a55-b271-ff62ed2f207d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=9{(y-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-563e7933-88b2-5d09-a466-e815264e47b5" :answer/id #uuid "563e7933-88b2-5d09-a466-e815264e47b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\frac{2}{3}{(y+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-781c4a5e-6128-5f7c-8d4d-bc8159e4a2de" :answer/id #uuid "781c4a5e-6128-5f7c-8d4d-bc8159e4a2de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\frac{2}{3}{(y-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e5de6f57-ca27-538b-8d1c-dacfab40980e" :answer/id #uuid "e5de6f57-ca27-538b-8d1c-dacfab40980e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\frac{3}{2}{(y-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186199500 :tutorial/content "Suppose we wish to find the points of intersection of the elliptic paraboloid \n$z=x^2+y^2$\nand the line with the equation\n$x = -y = -z+1.$\nThe line, paraboloid, and their points of intersection are shown below.\n\n![](images/51/5159ac99a1bc9f73c01df3c2cc2e6fb2093a3d68e00731609d7b62a6fa55149d.png)\n\n \n\nThe trick is to express the equation of the line in parametric form, substitute the parametric equations into the equation of the surface, and solve for the parameter.\n\nSo, first, we write the equation of our line in the parametric form:\n\n![](images/01/01357a5c6b72d7c976765aeed04db8afa3e3a80e13095d9be1ea2f2594ae5bf5.svg)\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\nOur intersection points must belong to the line and the surface simultaneously. So, substituting the expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ from the parametric equation of the line into the equation of the paraboloid, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & ={x}^{2}+{y}^{2} \\\\ (-t+1) & =(t)^{2}+(-t)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying this equation, we get\n\n$$\n2t^2+t - 1=0.\n$$\n\nThe solutions to this equation are\n$t=\\dfrac{1}{2}$ and $t=-1.$ \n\nSubstituting these values back into the parametric equations of the line\n\n- For $t=\\dfrac{1}{2}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ y=-(\\frac{1}{2})=-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ z=-(\\frac{1}{2})+1=\\frac{1}{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the first point is $(\\dfrac{1}{2},-\\dfrac{1}{2},\\dfrac{1}{2}).$\n\n- For $t=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=(-1)=-1 \\\\ y=-(-1)=1 \\\\ z=-(-1)+1=2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the second point is $(-1,1,2).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(\\dfrac{1}{2},-\\dfrac{1}{2},\\dfrac{1}{2})$ and $(-1,1,2).$ \n\nLet's see another example." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186199499 :tutorial/content "Now, let's consider the intersection of the elliptic paraboloid \n$z=x^2+y^2$\nand the plane \n$z = x+y-\\dfrac{1}{4},$\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/1d/1d4b8db0985d437807f6e580bc6c2c16cacca1ea7c8e49ed4653717cdb3c9e27.png)\n\n \n\nNote that the intersection of the paraboloid and plane is given by the solution to the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}z={x}^{2}+{y}^{2} \\\\ z=x+y-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\n- To find the projection of the intersection onto the $xy$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $z$ from the system. The resulting projection curve will be an ellipse, as depicted below.\n\n![](images/52/520b57cf872ede31d4397d59a833c565147d82a45be1d6b2634f82e1effdff8c.png)\n\n \n\n- To find the projection of the intersection onto the $xz$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $y$ from the system. The resulting projection curve will be an ellipse, as depicted below.\n\n![](images/05/059acf1ec5dadaa98b2cd4d4b6c79884e4facc96dd49664abbc247cfba86aaeb.png)\n\n \n\n- To find the projection of the intersection onto the $yz$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $x$ from the system. The resulting projection curve will be an ellipse, as depicted below.\n\n![](images/80/80d3042d21d2e7265a40739ae1531ac30b03fea16fa67609a4e1b0eac8559411.png)\n\n \n\nLet's see some examples." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198505 :activity/expected-seconds 900.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133911 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3d069a94-d7d6-5988-ba00-dc610c0a1a5e" "question-cf8a8a57-6cfe-5981-b026-15b496e6e0d3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133912 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-00ee9625-b07b-5511-af62-7520bef2fbbd"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133468 :question/problem "![](images/b3/b36961dd90e73504bf46d63827d1ea68292c01a7990f8fa3eb00eee62a4b1813.svg)\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0.$\n\nI. $A$ has a zero column\n\nII. $A$ has proportional rows\n\nIII. $A$ has identical columns" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-3d069a94-d7d6-5988-ba00-dc610c0a1a5e" :question/id #uuid "3d069a94-d7d6-5988-ba00-dc610c0a1a5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-82194" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ -7 & 1 & -1 & -7 \\\\ 3 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 3\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 0.5 \\\\ 3 & -3 & \\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has identical columns: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ -7 & 1 & -1 & -7 \\\\ 3 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|A|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 0.5 \\\\ 3 & -3 & \\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- Since $C$ is a triangular matrix, we obtain \n\n$$\n|C|=7\\cdot (-1)\\cdot (-2)=14\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $|A|$ and $|B|$ are equal to $0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-23681fe8-270b-5047-9929-75e3e8fd1007"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-23681fe8-270b-5047-9929-75e3e8fd1007" :answer-field/id #uuid "23681fe8-270b-5047-9929-75e3e8fd1007" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6c724853-4dc1-5954-a54d-2cd8c40b90e7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6c724853-4dc1-5954-a54d-2cd8c40b90e7" "answer-827c6d51-bd40-574d-b735-ef588e897657" "answer-2f2d0592-797e-5802-8ca4-8a2a42612d69" "answer-0277c4bf-919b-5267-9625-3ce886304e59" "answer-f04249bb-8ff4-5ab0-bd54-1f9f6f447fd3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6c724853-4dc1-5954-a54d-2cd8c40b90e7" :answer/id #uuid "6c724853-4dc1-5954-a54d-2cd8c40b90e7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-827c6d51-bd40-574d-b735-ef588e897657" :answer/id #uuid "827c6d51-bd40-574d-b735-ef588e897657" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f2d0592-797e-5802-8ca4-8a2a42612d69" :answer/id #uuid "2f2d0592-797e-5802-8ca4-8a2a42612d69" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$|A|$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0277c4bf-919b-5267-9625-3ce886304e59" :answer/id #uuid "0277c4bf-919b-5267-9625-3ce886304e59" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f04249bb-8ff4-5ab0-bd54-1f9f6f447fd3" :answer/id #uuid "f04249bb-8ff4-5ab0-bd54-1f9f6f447fd3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$|B|$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-cf8a8a57-6cfe-5981-b026-15b496e6e0d3" :question/id #uuid "cf8a8a57-6cfe-5981-b026-15b496e6e0d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-82193" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}5 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a triangular matrix, we obtain \n\n$$\n|A|=5\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 2=-10\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has a zero column: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has identical rows: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, only $|B|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a79e0fe4-97d1-5338-b5f9-fcb08969416e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a79e0fe4-97d1-5338-b5f9-fcb08969416e" :answer-field/id #uuid "a79e0fe4-97d1-5338-b5f9-fcb08969416e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a382ca9c-09f6-5fe7-ae8f-109968b53e3e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b4309380-2eb3-5ecd-b864-93456f98633e" "answer-cda12a20-ad57-5314-886c-4677c2cad21f" "answer-a382ca9c-09f6-5fe7-ae8f-109968b53e3e" "answer-1567e615-6ab4-5dfa-a4ee-bb5f68553e0c" "answer-ea65d58a-0ecc-516b-bd6b-912a169e765a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4309380-2eb3-5ecd-b864-93456f98633e" :answer/id #uuid "b4309380-2eb3-5ecd-b864-93456f98633e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cda12a20-ad57-5314-886c-4677c2cad21f" :answer/id #uuid "cda12a20-ad57-5314-886c-4677c2cad21f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|C|$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a382ca9c-09f6-5fe7-ae8f-109968b53e3e" :answer/id #uuid "a382ca9c-09f6-5fe7-ae8f-109968b53e3e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1567e615-6ab4-5dfa-a4ee-bb5f68553e0c" :answer/id #uuid "1567e615-6ab4-5dfa-a4ee-bb5f68553e0c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$|B|$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea65d58a-0ecc-516b-bd6b-912a169e765a" :answer/id #uuid "ea65d58a-0ecc-516b-bd6b-912a169e765a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$|C|$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-00ee9625-b07b-5511-af62-7520bef2fbbd" :question/id #uuid "00ee9625-b07b-5511-af62-7520bef2fbbd" :question/math-academy-id "q-82287" :question/problem "Find $5det(A)+2det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & -1 & 1.5 \\\\ 3 & -9 & 12\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has proportional rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & -1 & 1.5 \\\\ 3 & -9 & 12\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- For the matrix $B,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(B)=2\\cdot 3-\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $5det(A)+2det(B)=5\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 3=6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0ac158dd-e2ea-5d6f-9ec0-895c0248c590"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0ac158dd-e2ea-5d6f-9ec0-895c0248c590" :answer-field/id #uuid "0ac158dd-e2ea-5d6f-9ec0-895c0248c590" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b1e66de3-9711-58eb-a4b6-9c6f7f7d5114" :answer-field/choices ["answer-366bb306-e5b1-5bce-82a8-a14197bda5e2" "answer-cf227642-8c60-5fac-8a8c-4941679de5a8" "answer-5c836208-8886-5ac5-a42b-bc5298710b67" "answer-66dd1cc6-ae10-55ca-805b-f651571a416c" "answer-b1e66de3-9711-58eb-a4b6-9c6f7f7d5114"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-366bb306-e5b1-5bce-82a8-a14197bda5e2" :answer/id #uuid "366bb306-e5b1-5bce-82a8-a14197bda5e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf227642-8c60-5fac-8a8c-4941679de5a8" :answer/id #uuid "cf227642-8c60-5fac-8a8c-4941679de5a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c836208-8886-5ac5-a42b-bc5298710b67" :answer/id #uuid "5c836208-8886-5ac5-a42b-bc5298710b67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66dd1cc6-ae10-55ca-805b-f651571a416c" :answer/id #uuid "66dd1cc6-ae10-55ca-805b-f651571a416c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1e66de3-9711-58eb-a4b6-9c6f7f7d5114" :answer/id #uuid "b1e66de3-9711-58eb-a4b6-9c6f7f7d5114" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186135154 :tutorial/content "In conclusion, if an $n\\!\\times \\!n$ matrix $A$ satisfies any one of the following conditions, then $\\det(A)=0.$\n\nI. $A$ has a zero row/column\n\nII. $A$ has two identical rows/columns\n\nIII. $A$ has two proportional rows/columns\n\nIV. $A$ has a row/column that is a linear combination of other rows/columns\n\nNotice that condition IV encompasses each of the conditions I, II, and III. If we have a zero row/column, two identical rows/columns, or proportional rows/columns, then the rows/columns form a linearly dependent set of vectors. \nIn turn, this means that one of the rows/columns is a linear combination of other rows/columns.\n\n**Watch out!** While all of the above conditions are *sufficient* to conclude that $\\det(A)=0,$ only condition IV is *necessary* to conclude that $\\det(A)=0.$ \nIn other words, if we have a matrix $A$ with $\\det(A)=0,$ then conditions I, II, and III may or may not be satisfied, while condition IV *must* be satisfied. \n\nSo, we have the following theorem:\n\n*$\\det(A)=0$ if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nFinally, note also that in the case of a $2\\times 2$ matrix *only*, statements III and IV mean the same thing." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073879 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d691d9e9-ebc4-5231-9220-d7666a1593ac" "question-98f6bb07-5c0b-539a-985d-169696ff401a" "question-6e29d990-90ac-50f9-be81-d4fdf354bbe5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d691d9e9-ebc4-5231-9220-d7666a1593ac" :question/id #uuid "d691d9e9-ebc4-5231-9220-d7666a1593ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-60243" :question/problem "What is missing in the following sentence?\n\nA jar contains $7$ pounds of pinto beans and $9$ pounds of black beans, so there are $\\boxed{}$ pounds of pinto beans for each pound of black beans." :question/worked-solution "The ratio of the number of pounds of pinto beans to the number of pounds of black beans is  $7:9.$ \n\nWe can rewrite this ratio as a fraction, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{9}\n$$\n\nThis means that there are $\\frac{7}{9}$ pounds of pinto beans for each pound of black beans." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7a2a655e-4e9e-5995-b06a-a119a03f5ad9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7a2a655e-4e9e-5995-b06a-a119a03f5ad9" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a2a655e-4e9e-5995-b06a-a119a03f5ad9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-771b351c-dd76-56f5-b4b6-339322c69aa6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ec6a1468-df22-5e30-8c94-3e89caf0d05e" "answer-56e44c30-1084-5be2-a01c-ad2535a0461e" "answer-c9e132a2-99a9-53b3-9d7f-841eaa7b465a" "answer-771b351c-dd76-56f5-b4b6-339322c69aa6" "answer-ae8414db-6839-51e8-a990-fff4eccf5e80"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec6a1468-df22-5e30-8c94-3e89caf0d05e" :answer/id #uuid "ec6a1468-df22-5e30-8c94-3e89caf0d05e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{16}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56e44c30-1084-5be2-a01c-ad2535a0461e" :answer/id #uuid "56e44c30-1084-5be2-a01c-ad2535a0461e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9e132a2-99a9-53b3-9d7f-841eaa7b465a" :answer/id #uuid "c9e132a2-99a9-53b3-9d7f-841eaa7b465a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-771b351c-dd76-56f5-b4b6-339322c69aa6" :answer/id #uuid "771b351c-dd76-56f5-b4b6-339322c69aa6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae8414db-6839-51e8-a990-fff4eccf5e80" :answer/id #uuid "ae8414db-6839-51e8-a990-fff4eccf5e80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-98f6bb07-5c0b-539a-985d-169696ff401a" :question/id #uuid "98f6bb07-5c0b-539a-985d-169696ff401a" :question/math-academy-id "q-92937" :question/problem "What is missing in the following sentence?\n\nJason bought $2$ kilograms of almonds and $3$ kilograms of peanuts, so there are $\\boxed{}$ kilograms of almonds for each kilogram of peanuts." :question/worked-solution "The ratio of the amount of almonds to the amount of peanuts is  $2:3.$ \n\nWe can rewrite this ratio as a fraction, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}\n$$\n\nThis means that Jason has $\\frac{2}{3}$ kilograms of almonds for each kilogram of peanuts." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cea5214f-40d3-5c1e-a0c5-3dc1a765d0e0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cea5214f-40d3-5c1e-a0c5-3dc1a765d0e0" :answer-field/id #uuid "cea5214f-40d3-5c1e-a0c5-3dc1a765d0e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-eec0f341-30fb-5cd1-8791-3e5f4a008690" :answer-field/choices ["answer-54df06f8-3c9f-5eed-bae7-3446c807721e" "answer-5a746103-81b2-53bc-9279-877665fe7edb" "answer-ef1d8bd9-c716-5da7-8c9c-5e27a324273a" "answer-3e654a7b-3470-5939-83f9-19701e98a7a8" "answer-eec0f341-30fb-5cd1-8791-3e5f4a008690"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-54df06f8-3c9f-5eed-bae7-3446c807721e" :answer/id #uuid "54df06f8-3c9f-5eed-bae7-3446c807721e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a746103-81b2-53bc-9279-877665fe7edb" :answer/id #uuid "5a746103-81b2-53bc-9279-877